# ::tok " The amount of compensation is determined on a case - by - case basis and according to the circumstances , " says Attorney Reif - Liganza , and she adds and notes that " today , most claims on the grounds of medical negligence end in a compromise that weighs the chance and risk that each party has in conducting the procedure , " but the attorney added and said that " there are cases in which the procedure ends only with a judgment , then if the claim is not rejected , the plaintiffs will receive full compensation for all their damages and , for example , in a lawsuit conducted by our office , the district court awarded a minor who suffered cerebral palsy due to a delay in identifying fetal distress compensation in excess of ten million shekels . "
